%description:

A deviation of the TR 36.873 UMa environment height from the specification,
recorded rather than fixed (model deviation 26). TR 36.873 v12.7.0 Table
7.2-1 NOTE 4: "h_E=1m with a probability equal to 1/(1+C(d2D, hUT)) and
chosen from a discrete uniform distribution uniform(12,15,...,(hUT-1.5))
otherwise. The function C(d2D, hUT) is defined in Table 7.2-2. Note that h_E
depends on d2D and hUT and thus needs to be independently determined for
every link between BS sites and UTs."

Table 7.2-2 defines no C(d2D, hUT): it defines C'(hUT), 0 for hUT <= 13m and
((hUT-13)/10)^1.5 for 13m < hUT <= 23m, and uses it in the UMa LOS
probability as C'(hUT) 5/4 (d2D-out/100)^3 exp(-d2D-out/150). C(d2D, hUT) is
read as that term, at d2D and 0 for d2D <= 18 m, as pathloss_reference.py
does (_t873_c, "inferred, not quoted"): the note says h_E depends on d2D, and
TR 38.901 Table 7.4.1-1 NOTE 1 writes C(d2D, hUT) out so.
Tr36873PathLossModel::drawEnvironmentHeight() takes C'(hUT) alone, so the
probability of 1 m does not depend on the distance: at hUT = 22.5 m it is
0.52 everywhere, where the reading gives 0.98 at 30 m, 0.63 at 100 m and
0.29 at 200 m.

Graded from the frequencies of 40000 draws, as in PathLossEnvironmentHeight,
which pins the current distribution. When fixed, drop the %expected-failure
line, fold the cases into PathLossEnvironmentHeight and drop the pin there.

%expected-failure: the TR 36.873 h_E draw leaves out the distance term of C(d2D, hUT)

%includes:
#include <map>
#include "PathLossTestUtil.h"
#include "simu5g/stack/phy/channelmodel/Tr36873PathLossModel.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%activity:
CaseRecorder probe(this, 1e-6);
const int N = 40000;
const double heValues[] = { 1, 12, 15, 18, 21 };

ScenarioParams p;
p.scenario = URBAN_MACROCELL;
p.hNodeB = 25;
p.hUe = 22.5;
p.carrierFrequencyGHz = 0.8;
Deployed<Tr36873PathLossModel> m;
p.apply(m, this);

for (double d : { 30.0, 100.0, 200.0 }) {
    std::map<double, int> counts;
    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++)
        counts[m.drawEnvironmentHeight(d)]++;
    for (double v : heValues)
        probe.record("t873_p_he", p, { { "d2D", d }, { "hE", v } }, counts[v] / (double)N, 0.01);
}

probe.summary();

%postrun-command: ../../pathloss_reference.py --grade test.out >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=15 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
